<title>BELGIUM: EU raises &quot;C&quot; sugar carry-over, export forecasts.</title>
<headline>EU raises &quot;C&quot; sugar carry-over, export forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union carry-over of non-quota &quot;C&quot; sugar into the 1997/98 marketing season is expected to total 917,000 tonnes, up from 890,000 tonnes forecast last month, the European Commission said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Commission also raised its forecast of &quot;C&quot; sugar exports to 2.44 million tonnes in 1996/97, from a previous forecast of 2.28 million tonnes.  </p>
<p>The &quot;C&quot; sugar carry-over into 1996/97 totalled 685,000 tonnes while &quot;C&quot; sugar exports in 1995/96 amounted to 1.58 million tonnes.</p>
<p>&quot;Higher &quot;C&quot; sugar exports are due to increased production after an unexpectedly big crop,&quot; a Commission official said.</p>
<p>A revised EU sugar balance sheet, the 14th, was presented on Wednesday at the weekly meeting of the EU sugar management committee but discussion was postponed until next week.</p>
<p>EU beet sugar output was estimated at 16.52 million tonnes in 1996/97, compared with 16.34 million tonnes last month and 15.56 million in 1995/96.</p>
